  "opening": "Deutsch’s algorithm uses state preparation, an oracle, and a final interference step. A circuit describes how such operations are assembled from elementary gates acting on one or two qubits. Their construction determines costs that an oracle query count alone does not include.",
  "opening_continuation": [
    "We begin with circuit notation and controls, then construct single-qubit gates, controlled gates, phase oracles, and reflections. Universality describes which operations a gate set can build or approximate. Gate count, depth, workspace, connectivity, and accumulated error describe the resources required.",
    "These constructions supply the operations used next in quantum search and amplitude amplification."
  ]
